    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, please have a seat. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Hi, yeah, thanks. Um, well, I guess what brings me in is... I just feel like I’ve got this motor humming under my skin whenever I’m supposed to sit still. Like, if I'm in a staff meeting at work—I'm a building cleaner over at the community college. I actually used to work over at the high school, but man, the kids there leave such a mess with those sticky energy drinks they all drink now. You know the ones? They spill them everywhere and it just eats right through the commercial floor wax. I used to spend half my shift just buffing out those sticky spots. \n\nBut anyway, yeah, in our staff meetings, or like during church event briefings, I just... I end up shifting around constantly, or I have to stand up, or I just find some excuse to go check a hallway or move around. The pastor actually stopped his briefing last week because I was pacing in the back. He's a good guy, Pastor Dave. His wife makes this incredible potato salad for the summer potlucks, she puts a little paprika in it, I think, or maybe it's dill... but yeah, sitting still just doesn't really work for me.",
