    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Aside from feeling restless, do you also struggle with staying focused when you have to work on a task?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Focus? Um, no, I don't think so. Not really. If I have a task to do, I can usually just do it, especially if I'm working with my hands. Like yesterday, I was fixing the hinges on this heavy oak door over in the science building. Those doors are massive, they must weigh two hundred pounds easy. They just don't make doors like that anymore, you know? Now everything is that cheap hollow core stuff. You knock on it and it sounds like cardboard. \n\nMy buddy Al—he works over at the hardware store on 4th street—he says they don't even stock solid wood doors anymore because the freight shipping costs are just completely out of control. It's crazy what they charge to ship things now. I ordered a replacement belt for my vacuum cleaner last month, just a little loop of rubber, right? And the shipping was more than the belt itself! It’s a Sanitaire vacuum, one of those tough red ones with the big cloth bag. Best machine ever made, honestly, it'll suck up a whole hex nut if you aren't careful. I’ve had to fish so many paperclips out of the roller brush... \n\nBut, uh... wait, what were we talking about? Oh, right, staying focused. Yeah, no, I don't really have a problem focusing on the work itself. I just have to be on my feet doing it.",
