    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often find yourself misplacing or losing things you need, like your keys, wallet, or tools?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Losing things? No, not really. I mean, I keep everything pretty organized. You kind of have to in my line of work, especially with the keys. I have this huge ring of master keys for the college, and if you lose that, oh boy. The whole campus has to be rekeyed. That happened to a guy I knew, Gary. Gary was a good guy, but he left his keys on the bumper of his truck and just drove off. He drove this old Ford Ranger, one of those little boxy ones from the nineties. The paint was peeling off the hood in these big flakes, looked like a bad sunburn. He tried to touch it up with spray paint once, but he bought the wrong shade of blue, so it looked even worse. \n\nBut yeah, the college had to spend thousands of dollars changing every lock in the humanities building because of Gary. They actually put those electronic keycard scanners on the new science wing after that. Which, honestly, I hate those things. Half the time the scanner doesn't read the card, or the battery dies in the door mechanism and you're just locked out anyway. Give me a good old-fashioned brass key any day. Brass is a great metal, you know? It doesn't rust. My grandfather had this solid brass compass he brought back from the war... but anyway, no, I don't really lose my tools or my wallet or anything. I keep my wallet in my front pocket, always have.",
